# `<path> <name>`). deep-deps mounts each of these RECURSIVELY
# DEEPENED at DEEP-DEPS/<name> (design/caos-expr.md).
#
# `rgrep` on purpose, not `bash`: rgrep is a rustc-built worker, so it
# resolves to curry(runner, worker1=<binary>) and its unwrapped base is
# the RUNNER POOL IMAGE — which is exactly the shape this test is about
# (see cli.sh). A flake-built image like bash's is pinned as a run
# result and so cannot exhibit it.
../../std/rgrep rgrep
../../std/runner runner
../../std/rustc rustc
